## THE WORK IN ONE SENTENCE (property first)
**Property:** after `frame()` returns, for each of the 19 frames, every call the page makes to load its content has answered and the content the rows read is on the screen, established ONLY by Playwright web-first assertions on what the page shows (`await expect(locator).toBeVisible()`, `toHaveCount`, `toHaveText`): no fixed time, no network-quiet heuristic, and no per-wait timeout longer than the config's. **At least these are forbidden** (any other shape: prove it is a condition on what the page shows, or STOP): `waitForTimeout`, `setTimeout`, `waitForLoadState` (any state, `networkidle` above all), `expect.poll`, `.toPass(`, `waitForFunction`, `.only`, `.skip`, `test.fixme`, `test.slow`, `test.setTimeout`, `retries`, a raised `{ timeout: ... }`, a loosened or removed expectation, a changed layout figure. **Shape (D-1, accepted unless slot S10 changes it):** `frame()` takes the page's readiness as a REQUIRED argument with no default (`frame(page, path, ready, width = 1280)`), so a new frame without a wait does not type-check and the 500 ms branch (`:25-26`) is deleted; ONE named wait per page, beside `dashboardData` (which keeps its three conditions as they are and is also the wait of `:63`): `homeData`, `workspaceData`, `documentsData`, and for the three static pages one named wait each (`designSystemReady`, `managedReady`, `revenueReady`) that waits for the page's own content (its h1 and the element its rows read), each with the failure message naming what it waited for (as `dashboardData`'s messages do). `homeData`: BOTH calls answered (no status whose text contains "Loading" inside `main#main`, plus the pipeline table's first row and the customers tile visible). `workspaceData`: the "Loading customers" status filtered by TEXT is gone and the list's heading and first row are visible (never a bare status count: trap 3). `documentsData`: the "Loading the customer's result" status filtered by text is gone and the customer's name is in the preview. Print, for each page, the full list of `role=status` elements in `main#main` at the settled state at the base (your own browser read) before you write a wait that depends on them.
**One test file. No product byte. No layout figure changes.** Every existing row keeps its title, its selector, its positive control and its expected value (`toBe`, `toEqual`, `toBeGreaterThan(...)`): the diff's removed lines are the frame definition, the 500 ms branch, and the 18 call lines (each now names a wait), and nothing else; any removed line holding `toBe(`, `toEqual(` or `toBeGreaterThan` counts 0 (control: a planted edit of one expected value counts 1).

